Hi Phil and Jean,

I do not know of any specific motherboard that can be bought separately with the ADM1032 on it. They typically have gone into Notebooks, XBox etc where the motherboards are generally not sold separately.

The general idea of our eval boards is to provide a simple environment that system designers can use to figure out how to program and use our devices.

They can generally be connected either through the DIMMs or PCI slots to a motherboard SMBus and can therefore be accessed by the motherboard. Our latest eval boards have an edge that can be slotted into a PCI slot to access the SMBus (when available on the PCI) and power these are not released yet.

Basically if you need any eval boards or samples let me know and I'll do what I can to get you one.

I was talking with Mary Burke who has also supported you, we both work in the same department so just let either one of us know if you need anything.

